home-assistant-gateway-1  | 2026-09-21T19:18:55.972303571Z {"event":"subagent_completed","requestId":6,"index":2,"attempt":1,"rounds":4,"answerCharacters":1572,"answer":"## The Spice Girls\n\n**Overview:** A British girl group formed in **1994**, consisting of:\n\n| Nickname | Member |\n|----------|--------|\n| Posh Spice | Victoria Beckham |\n| Scary Spice | Mel B |\n| Sporty Spice | Melanie C |\n| Ginger Spice | Geri Halliwell |\n| Baby Spice | Emma Bunton |\n\n**Key Facts:**\n\n- **Origin:** London, England; formed by Heart Management through auditions to compete with British boy bands. After leaving Heart, they hired Simon Fuller as manager and signed with Virgin Records.\n- **Debut:** \"Wannabe\" (1996) reached #1 in 37 countries. Their debut album *Spice* (1996) sold over 23 million copies worldwide, making them the best-selling album by a female group in history.\n- **Peak era:** They led the teen pop resurgence of the 1990s and were major icons of Cool Britannia. Their \"girl power\" mantra redefined the girl group concept with targeted young female fanbases.\n- **Touring:** The 1998 *Spiceworld Tour* was the highest-grossing concert tour by a female group, attended by ~2.1 million people. They set a record for most UK number-one singles by a girl group (9).\n- **Hiatus & Return:** Halliwell left in 1998. The group reunited for the *Return of the Spice Girls Tour* (2007), performed at the 2012 London Olympics closing ceremony, and toured again in 2019 (*Spice World ΓÇö 2019 UK Tour*).\n- **Awards:** Five Brit Awards, three American Music Awards, four Billboard Music Awards, three MTV Europe Music Awards, one MTV Video Music Award. In 2000 they became the youngest recipients of the Brit Award for Outstanding Contribution to Music.","evidenceSegments":1,"status":"complete","unresolved":[],"malformed":false,"executionSeconds":34.77014984000009}
