home-assistant-gateway-1  | 2026-09-21T19:22:53.220439103Z {"event":"research_reduce_completed","requestId":6,"inputCount":5,"answerCharacters":1560,"answer":"```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Victoria Beckham\",\n    \"nickname\": \"Posh Spice\",\n    \"birthday\": \"1974/04/17\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Mel B\",\n    \"nickname\": \"Scary Spice\",\n    \"birthday\": \"1975/05/29\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Melanie C\",\n    \"nickname\": \"Sporty Spice\",\n    \"birthday\": \"1974/01/12\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Geri Halliwell\",\n    \"nickname\": \"Ginger Spice\",\n    \"birthday\": \"1972/08/06\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Emma Bunton\",\n    \"nickname\": \"Baby Spice\",\n    \"birthday\": \"1976/01/21\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**The Spice Girls** are a British girl group formed in **London, England** in **1994**. They were originally formed by Heart Management through auditions to compete with British boy bands. After leaving Heart, they hired Simon Fuller as their manager and signed with Virgin Records.\n\nThey released their debut single **\"Wannabe\"** in 1996, which reached #1 in 37 countries. Their debut album *Spice* (1996) sold over **23 million copies worldwide**, making them the best-selling album by a female group in history. With their \"girl power\" mantra and targeted marketing toward young women, they led the teen pop resurgence of the 1990s and became major icons of Cool Britannia.\n\nThe 1998 *Spiceworld Tour* was the highest-grossing concert tour by a female group, attended by approximately **2.1 million people**. They set a record for most UK number-one singles by a girl group (9). Geri Halliwell left in 1998, and the group reunited for the *Return of the Spice Girls Tour* (2007), performed at the 2012 London Olympics closing ceremony, and toured again in 2019."}
